Using a decorator for memoization is an effective way to optimize recursive algorithms by avoiding redundant calculations. Here is the implementation:

def memoize(func):
    cache = {}
    def wrapper(*args):
        if args not in cache:
            cache[args] = func(*args)
        return cache[args]
    return wrapper

@memoize
def fib(n):
    if n < 2: return n
    return fib(n-1) + fib(n-2)

This approach shifts the time complexity from exponential O(2^n) to linear O(n).

